      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "The [[write-journal]] page describes **how the guarded write path journals prior file state for rollback on failure**.\n\nSpecifically, it explains:\n\n- **Before any write**: Before the guarded tool executor overwrites a file, it records the file\u0027s prior state\u2014either its previous content (if it existed) or the fact that it didn\u0027t exist\u2014into an in-memory write journal.\n\n- **Rollback on failure**: If the agent run fails (whether from hitting a turn cap, an unrecoverable error, or denied writes), the journal can roll back every recorded write in reverse order\u2014restoring previous content for existing files or deleting newly created ones.\n\n- **All-or-nothing semantics**: This design gives each run all-or-nothing semantics for its writes without needing a database transaction. The journal itself serves as the transaction log, held only in process memory for the duration of one run.\n\n- **Query agent note**: The Query agent never uses the rollback path since it has no write capability at all, though the journal type exists in the shared runtime library.",
      "input_tokens": 5553,
      "output_tokens": 236
    }
